  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed building by reason of its\nexcessive depth, bulk and siting would result in an inappropriate design and\nform of development that would constitute overdevelopment of the site and would\nbe incongruous and at odds with the character of the area and the prevailing\npattern of development in the streetscene, contrary to the high quality design\naspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D3 (D 1)\nand (D 11) of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core\nStrategy (2012), policy DM 1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies\nLocal Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential\nDesign Guide (2010). ",
    "The proposal, by reason of excessive\nsub-division of the rear amenity space, the isolated nature of the amenity\nspace from the proposed building and its poor quality access arrangements from\nthe main building to the communal amenity space would be at odds with the\nprevailing pattern of existing development in the area, result in a poor\nquality residential environment for future occupiers and would be contrary to the high quality design aspirations of\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies D3 (D1) and (D11) of The\nLondon Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of The Harrow Core Strategy (2012) and\nPolicies DM1 and DM27 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan\n(2013).",
    "The proposal would result\nin a net loss of biodiversity found on site and no mitigation measures have\nbeen submitted to either address the loss or to secure a net gain in biodiversity\non site. As such, the proposal would be detrimental to the local area and\nenvironment, contrary to Policy G6 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.E of The Harrow Core Strategy\n(2012) and Policy DM20 of\nthe Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013)."
  ],
